# Network binaries stay out: the weights are NVIDIA-derived and the runtime comes from a
# third-party project with its own distribution terms. Whoever clones brings their own.
# (See README, "Getting the runtime and the weights".)
#
# Third-party HEADERS are the opposite: they are vendored in 3rdparty/reshade/ so a fresh
# clone builds with nothing else to download. See 3rdparty/reshade/NOTICE.md.
*.dll
*.bin
*.addon64
*.exe
*.obj
*.lib
*.exp
*.pdb

# Build and run output
build/
builds/
build-x86bridge/
release/
release-v*/
local-x86-mod-package/
*.zip
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
diagnostic-logs-backup/
dlss5-runtime-v*/
*.log
*.ppm
*.raw

# One-off scratch scripts at the repository root, no value to anyone cloning. Anchored to the
# root on purpose: unanchored, patch_*.py matches at any depth and shadowed
# tools/patch_runtime.py, which the README documents as the way to rebuild the runtime.
/patch_*.py
/check_ppm.py

# Whatever the x86 installer writes into a directory it manages, plus the manual backup
# folders used while validating a game by hand. None of it is source.
dlss5-x86bridge.install.json
.dlss5-x86bridge-backups/
.dlss5-manual-backups/

# Editor and Windows shell noise
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.claude/settings.json
